// Shared by parse_if, parse_while, parse_switch and do_cond: `advance;
// advance; parse_expr` reads the '(cond)' after a keyword. Each caller
// already spends its whole 3-action budget on the rest of its body, leaving
// no room to read the condition inline. ctl/ has no room for a sibling
// file, so loop.id was promoted into this directory to make room.

read_paren_cond(int[] pos) {
  advance(pos);
  advance(pos);
  int a = parse_expr(pos);
} return int a;
